// A tree from its leaves (Inputs/river.ent): every node passes what it
// has gathered on to the node it flows into, with `+=` and `max=` through
// a `mut` binding up the tree, in a `for` that cascades `leaves first`.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/river.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/river.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// The nodes are spawned downstream first: in that order the sea would get
// the river's own 10 and no more.
// CHECK:      sea 11111 from 900
// CHECK-NEXT: river 11110 from 900
// CHECK-NEXT: brook 11000 from 900
// CHECK-NEXT: spring 10000 from 900
// CHECK-NEXT: creek 100 from 500
// CHECK-NEXT: lake 5 from 50
// Children before their parents: the nodes from the one connected last
// to the first, which every node's parent was there before; then those
// without a parent.
// CHECK-NEXT: visit creek
// CHECK-NEXT: visit spring
// CHECK-NEXT: visit brook
// CHECK-NEXT: visit river
// CHECK-NEXT: visit sea
// CHECK-NEXT: visit lake
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
